    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0268" n="196" xml:id="pg196"/>

                <head>No. 104.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-02-04"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 4, 1882</date>.
                        (Received February 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 305.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 300, of the
                    30th ultimo, I have the honor to inclose the copy of a letter which I received
                    this morning, in which Lord Granville states that the lord lieutenant of Ireland
                    has expressed regret that he cannot, consistently with his duty, order the
                    release of Mr. Denis Hayes O’Connor at present.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d104-a1.xml" xpointer="d104-a1"/>
            </div>
